.TH CAGE 1 "2026-08-19" "cage 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cage \- confine one command with the host kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cage
.RB [ \-net ]
.RB [ \-ro | " \-w " dir ...]
.B \--
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B cage check
.br
.B cage status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cage
runs one child process under the host operating system's filesystem and
network boundary.
The child may read the host filesystem.
By default it may write the current directory and temporary directory, and
cannot reach host networks.
.PP
Standard input, standard output, and standard error pass through unchanged.
Ordinary child exit status passes through unchanged.
A backend may represent signal termination using 128 plus the signal number;
Cage preserves that convention.
Backend readiness has a five-second deadline; child runtime is not limited.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-net
Permit host networking.
Without this option host and public networks are denied.
Linux may retain loopback inside an isolated network namespace.
.TP
.B \-ro
Do not grant write access to the current directory.
The temporary directory remains writable.
.TP
.BI \-w " dir"
Grant write access beneath an existing directory.
May be repeated.
Once present, the current directory is not implicitly writable.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-ro .
.TP
.B \--
End Cage options.
Recommended before every command and required when its name starts with a
hyphen.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Attempt workspace writes, denied outside writes, read-only and explicit-write
modes, default network denial, deliberate networking, standard-input
preservation, exit and signal propagation, and fail-closed setup.
.TP
.B status
Write one JSON record describing platform, backend, availability, and
enforcement completeness.
An unavailable status is still a successful query; running a child then
fails with 125.
.TP
.B version
Print the Cage version.
.TP
.B help
Print a command summary.
.SH BACKENDS
.SS macOS
Uses Seatbelt through
.BR /usr/bin/sandbox-exec .
.SS Linux
Uses Bubblewrap from a trusted absolute system path.
The root is mounted read-only, selected roots are rebound read-write, and a
private device filesystem and locked user namespace are created, capabilities
are dropped, and a network namespace is created unless
.B \-net
is present.
.SS Windows and other platforms
Refuses with status 125 because this release has no complete native backend.
Use Windows Sandbox or a container with explicit mounts and network policy.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The child succeeded, or a status/help/version/check query succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
At least one
.B cage check
assertion failed, or the child returned 1.
.TP
.B 2
Cage usage error, or the child returned 2.
.TP
.B 125
Confinement setup failed and the requested child did not start, or the child
itself returned 125.
Cage setup failures include a
.B confinement setup
diagnostic on standard error.
.TP
.B other
The child's status.
.SH SECURITY
Cage restricts writes and networking, not reads, identity, CPU, memory,
process count, elapsed time, output, human approval, or credentials.
The temporary directory is writable.
.B \-net
permits all host networking and is not a destination allowlist.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Writable temporary directory.
Set it before Cage to select a private scratch root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cage -- go test ./...
cage -ro -- inspector source.tar
cage -w ./build -w ./generated -- make all
cage -net -- curl https://example.com
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bwrap (1),
.BR sandbox-exec (1)
